      "slots": [
        {
          "component": "section-label",
          "block": "",
          "text": "CONTEXT",
          "label": "",
          "provenance": "",
          "path": "",
          "rank": "label",
          "step": "t2",
          "cap_mm": 2.5,
          "emphasis": false,
          "x_mm": 0.0,
          "y_mm": 0.0,
          "width_mm": 38.75,
          "height_mm": 10.0,
          "columns": 1,
          "ink": 0.18
        },
        {
          "component": "body",
          "block": "nar-01",
          "text": "A 1904 malthouse on the edge of the town's former industrial quarter, built to germinate barley on three timber floors and abandoned in 1987. The brick shell is sound and the cast-iron columns are intact. The roof is not: two bays collapsed in the winter of 2019 and the remainder was condemned in the survey that followed.",
          "label": "",
          "provenance": "",
          "path": "",
          "rank": "body",
          "step": "t2",
          "cap_mm": 2.5,
          "emphasis": false,
          "x_mm": 43.75,
          "y_mm": 0.0,
          "width_mm": 126.25,
          "height_mm": 25.0,
          "columns": 3,
          "ink": 0.18
        },
        {
          "component": "body",
          "block": "fct-07",
          "text": "3",
          "label": "Storeys",
          "provenance": "",
          "path": "",
          "rank": "body",
          "step": "t2",
          "cap_mm": 2.5,
          "emphasis": false,
          "x_mm": 43.75,
          "y_mm": 30.0,
          "width_mm": 126.25,
          "height_mm": 20.0,
          "columns": 3,
          "ink": 0.18
        },
        {
          "component": "body",
          "block": "fct-08",
          "text": "24",
          "label": "Spaces",
          "provenance": "",
          "path": "",
          "rank": "body",
          "step": "t2",
          "cap_mm": 2.5,
          "emphasis": false,
          "x_mm": 43.75,
          "y_mm": 55.0,
          "width_mm": 126.25,
          "height_mm": 20.0,
          "columns": 3,
          "ink": 0.18
        },
        {
          "component": "body",
          "block": "nar-03",
          "text": "A new steel frame stands inside the shell on independent pads, carrying the new floors clear of the historic masonry. The original timber floors are retained where sound and read as a second, lighter layer beneath the new. Insulation is applied internally to the gables only, leaving the north elevation as found and taking the heat loss on the plant instead.",
          "label": "",
          "provenance": "",
          "path": "",
          "rank": "body",
          "step": "t2",
          "cap_mm": 2.5,
          "emphasis": false,
          "x_mm": 43.75,
          "y_mm": 80.0,
          "width_mm": 126.25,
          "height_mm": 25.0,
          "columns": 3,
          "ink": 0.18
        },
        {
          "component": "figure",
          "block": "drw-01",
          "text": "Long section 1:100. New frame shown at the cut weight.",
          "label": "",
          "provenance": "",
          "path": "projects/malthouse/A3-201-section.pdf",
          "rank": "caption",
          "step": "t1",
          "cap_mm": 1.8,
          "emphasis": false,
          "x_mm": 0.0,
          "y_mm": 110.0,
          "width_mm": 170.0,
          "height_mm": 135.0,
          "columns": 4,
          "ink": 0.0
        }
      ],
      "fill_ratio": 0.7942,
      "ink_coverage_max": 0.18,
      "alignment_edges_x": 4,
